        },
        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for lod_set_pool",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for lod_set_pool\n\nAdd lod_pool_test.ko, exercising lod_set_pool(): setting a pool name\nfrom NULL, replacing an existing one, the @*pool == @new_pool\nshort-circuit used by lod_obj_set_pool() when nothing changed, and\nclearing a pool back to NULL. It is a small, self-contained string\nhelper with no dt_object/OST/thandle involved, used here as a worked\nexample of mapping a kunit module to a single function via\nKUNIT.list's new \"<glob>:<function>\" syntax, rather than the\nwhole-directory \"*.[ch]\" glob the other lod kunit modules use.\n\nAlso cover the OST pool registry itself, via a real (but device/OSD\nfree) lod_device: lod_pool_exists(), lod_pool_find(), lod_find_pool()\n(the latter also rejecting an empty pool) and lod_check_index_in_pool()\nagainst a pool created with lod_pool_new(), and lod_qos_set_pool(),\nwhich resolves a component's requested pool name and clamps its\nstripe count to the pool's target count. Export the lod_pool.c\nhelpers and lod_qos_set_pool() for direct testing.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5\nChange-Id: Iec38900db232d194cc1f2db49bf5c5cadf137b98\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
